From e8f8d3b2cecd89369f9ed519f89a6ae5a02b2e43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dylanoliverdo-coder
 <265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:11:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf(sim): grow the column stock's cut history in place

cut::simulate copied the stock's whole cut history at the start of each
call. A caller that cuts one move for each call thus copied a longer
history at each step, and the time was quadratic in the moves.

The history is now taken out, grown with Arc::make_mut (a copy only when
another stock shares it) and put back. On a refusal, the cuts are
truncated to their old count and the history goes back, because add_ops
only appends cuts.

Pinned by stock_sim::cut::history_tests (the history keeps its
allocation across calls; a clone keeps its own history and columns) and
stock_columns::one_move_for_each_call_is_the_one_call_cut (4000
one-move calls give the one-call stock to the bit).

Fixes #3819

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
